-- title:
--   A level-p twist of the X₁(Mp) function field
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the image under coefficientwise extension $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ (`coeffEmb`) of the field `x1FunctionField (M * p)` $\subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$, assumed nonzero, whose underlying Laurent series is the image of the $q$-expansion `jq` $= q^{-1}\cdot(\text{power series } jNumQ)$ of the modular invariant. Then there is an $L$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $K$ with four properties. First, the Laurent series underlying $\sigma j$ is the image of `qExpand ℚ p jq`, the $q \mapsto q^{p}$ substitution applied to `jq`. Second, $\sigma$ preserves, in both directions, the subalgebra `chartAlgFin A K j` of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$. Third, for every valuation subring $W_0$ of $K$ which is characterised by the property that $f \in W_0$ exactly when there are power series $x, y$ over $A$ with $y$ nonzero modulo the maximal ideal and $f \cdot y_L = x_L$ in $L((q))$ (the Gauss branch), the preimage $\sigma^{-1}W_0$ differs from $W_0$, yet contains both $P(j)$ and $P(j)^{-1}$ for every $P \in A[X]$ whose reduction modulo the maximal ideal is nonzero. Fourth, for every $f$ in `modularFunctionFieldFull (M * p)`, the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the series `qExpand ℚ d jq` for nonzero divisors $d$ of $Mp$, whose image under `coeffEmb` lies in $K$, the element $\sigma$ sends that image to is the image of `atkinLehnerInvolutionFull M p f`, i.e. of the value at $f$ of a chosen $\mathbb{Q}$-automorphism of `modularFunctionFieldFull (M * p)` interchanging `qExpand ℚ d jq` with `qExpand ℚ (d * p) jq` for all nonzero $d \mid M$ (the identity if no such automorphism exists).
--
--   This is the construction of the degree-$p$ twisting automorphism of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_p)$, realised on $q$-expansions as $q \mapsto q^{p}$ on $j$ and as the partial Atkin–Lehner involution $w_p$ on the subfield generated by the expansions $j(q^{d})$, $d \mid Mp$. It is used in the analysis of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over a discrete valuation ring above $p$: the second and third clauses say that $\sigma$ preserves the chart finite over the $j$-line while moving the Gauss branch above the generic point of that line in characteristic $p$, which is what the subsequent statements on valuation subrings and minimal primes of the model invoke.
